WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.709
The first known boat to

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:02.669
actually navigate underwater was,

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.879
of course, built by a Dutch dude.

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:05.547
The Dutch, man.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:06.840
They're just so good at water.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.925
150 years later, over here,

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.094
in what was soon to be the United States,

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.470
George Washington paid

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.764
for this sucker to be made for his army.

00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:15.598
The Turtle,

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.183
because it kind of looked like two turtle

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.643
shells put together. So cute.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:20.186
The guy in there is just like so cozy.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.480
They tried to use “the turtle” in their war

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.024
for freedom against the British,

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.734
but it never really did anything useful.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.193
And then it just sank

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:27.736
cool name

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:30.030
but wasn't a super useful submarine

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.905
but it paved the way.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:31.865
50 years later,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.366
we have the American Civil War,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.410
where the Confederate rebels built a sub

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.995
that was powered by a bunch of guys

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:39.164
manually turning a crank and on board

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:41.166
it had a long spar torpedo.

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:42.042
Don’t be fooled, though

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.585
“spar torpedo” is just a fancy way

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:46.046
of saying a bomb on a 15 foot stick.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.047
And they actually used it.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.506
They snuck up on a Yankee ship

00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:49.799
with their bomb stick

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.217
in the middle of the Civil War

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.302
and blew it up.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:54.137
And both sides sank.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.680
Like, the submarine sank too.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.556
Like, it didn't work.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.767
I mean, it kind of worked, but it–

00:00:58.767 --> 00:00:59.350
didn't really work.

